{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2078245,"ns":0,"title":"Baire space (set theory)","extract":"In set theory, the Baire space is the set of all infinite sequences of natural numbers. This space is commonly used in descriptive set theory, to the extent that its elements are often called \"reals\".","description":"Concept in set theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}